### Page 2 of 3

```text
1
RESOLUTION NO. ________

ENTITLED: “A
RESOLUTION
AUTHORIZING
THE
SUBMISSION
OF
AN
APPLICATION TO THE WYOMING BUSINESS COUNCIL BUSINESS
READY COMMUNITY GRANT AND LOAN PROGRAM FOR A
$3,000,000.00 COMMUNITY READINESS GRANT,
AND UP TO
$3,000,000.00 IN BUSINESS READY COMMUNITY LOAN FUNDING,
FOR THE HAPPY JACK ROAD/F.E. WARREN AIR FORCE BASE
ENHANCED USE LEASE INFRASTRUCTURE PROJECT.”

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne recognizes the need for the
construction of critical water and sewer infrastructure to allow for the creation of a significant
mixed use development to provide vital housing and services to the Cheyenne Community and
personnel of F.E. Warren Air Force Base, as one of the region’s most significant employers; and

WHEREAS, this infrastructure project proposes preparing a 75.3 acre parcel with
necessary water and sewer public infrastructure and roadway improvements associated with
public right-of-way to allow for the construction of as much as $95 million in private residential
and commercial construction, which is estimated will generate $294,000.00 in additional real
estate taxes and $4,200,000.00 in sales tax per year; and

WHEREAS, the specific goals and measures of success of this project are:

•
Construction of 12,000 linear feet of water mains.

•
Construction of 11,400 linear feet of sewer mains.

•
Construction of roadway improvements associated with public right-of-way.

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne desires to participate in the
Business Ready Community Grant and Loan Program (BRC) to assist in financing this project;
and

WHEREAS, the BRC requires that certain criteria be met, as described in the Wyoming
Business Council’s Rules governing the program, and to the best of our knowledge, this
application meets those criteria; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne plans to provide cash match to
this BRC Business Committed project from the following source(s):

A cash match of up to $3,000,000.00 coming from a BRC Loan from the
Wyoming Business Council; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne has a comprehensive operation
and maintenance plan including projected expenses and project income sources extending the life
of the assets; and

WHEREAS, as a public infrastructure project, the Governing Body of the City of
Cheyenne does not anticipate revenue beyond tapping and user fees that will be used to maintain
public infrastructure locally; and

WHEREAS, in the event of any project cost overruns, the City of Cheyenne will provide
funding in the amount necessary to complete the project utilizing the general or reserve funds of
the City; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne has considered other possible
funding solutions for this project which included additional funding from the private developer;
and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne is working in partnership with F.E. Warren Air Force
By Alessandra McCoy at 10:58 am, Feb 08, 2018
```

